sparky-stereo-screensavers (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every text of the page can be read: 4.5:1 or more against its ground
    (WCAG 2.2, 1.4.3) in any colour scheme. The quieter texts (the counts
    line, the "3D" and "2D" marks, "Not offered", the credit, the hints, the
    search field's placeholder, the note about a missing video background)
    keep the scheme's dim colour only where that reaches 4.5:1 and are moved
    towards the scheme's normal text by the smallest step otherwise; the
    selected row's texts are judged on the selection's colour the same way.
    Measured in the edition's default look and in Breeze Light and Dark.
  * The texts on the page's ground take the view's colours, the ground the
    page is drawn on.
  * The small preview stays a pair when the column beside the list has a
    scroll bar: the column keeps room for the bar, and the preview is never
    wider than the column shows. In a KDE session with the edition's look on
    a 1280x800 screen 0.1.0 showed one view with "The preview does not fit in
    the window".
  * A proof aid, off unless asked for: SPARKY_SAVER_TEXT_REPORT=FILE writes
    where every text of the page is and the colour it asks for.

 -- Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000

sparky-stereo-screensavers (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Screensavers page of System Settings (queue row 96; Daniel Ramos,
    2026-10-14 and 2026-11-24): every screensaver in one list, a small live
    preview, a full-screen preview, the show's choices and times, links to the
    pages around it. The layout is the one of KDE's retired Screen Saver
    module (kde-workspace 4.11, kcontrol/screensaver).
  * The launcher "Stereo Screensavers" moves here from gl-stereo-savers and
    opens the page.
  * Ten languages; a first draft made with AI assistance, pending native
    speakers.

 -- Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0000
